.TH EUCLID-CLI-EKM 1 "August 2026" "euclid-cli 1.18.37" "Euclid CLI Manual"
.SH NAME
euclid-cli-ekm \- manage Euclid encryption keys
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B euclid-cli
[\fB\-\-endpoint\fR \fIURL\fR]
[\fB\-\-loglevel\fR \fILEVEL\fR]
.B ekm
.I action
[\fIaction-options\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B ekm
module talks to the Euclid gateway's ekm service to create and list
encryption keys. Every
.B ekm
command sends a single JSON request to the gateway
(\fB\-\-endpoint\fR, default \fIhttps://localhost:5566\fR) and prints the
JSON response on success.
.PP
All
.B ekm
commands require the caller to be authenticated; see
.B AUTHENTICATION
below for how the session used to sign these requests is obtained.
.SH ACTIONS
.TP
.B create-key
Creates a new key with a given algorithm and length. See
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1).
.TP
.B list-keys
Lists existing keys, paged and sorted. See
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1).
.SH GLOBAL OPTIONS
These options are given to
.B euclid-cli
itself, before the
.I ekm
module name.
.TP
.BR \-e ", " \-\-endpoint " " \fIURL\fR
Euclid gateway endpoint to talk to, e.g. \fIhttps://localhost:5566\fR.
.TP
.BR \-\-ca\-cert " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a PEM CA certificate to trust in addition to the system trust
store, e.g. for self-signed development certificates.
.TP
.BR \-c ", " \-\-config " " \fIPATH\fR
Path to a JSON configuration file providing defaults for action
options (currently used by
.BR euclid-cli-esm (1)
only). Defaults to
.IR /usr/local/euclid/etc/euclid.json ;
silently ignored if the file doesn't exist.
.TP
.BR \-l ", " \-\-loglevel " " \fILEVEL\fR
Log level: one of \fItrace\fR, \fIdebug\fR, \fIinfo\fR, \fIwarning\fR,
\fIerror\fR, \fIfatal\fR. Defaults to \fIinfo\fR.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print top-level usage and exit.
.TP
.BR \-v ", " \-\-version
Print the euclid-cli version and exit.
.SH AUTHENTICATION
.B ekm
commands are authenticated using the session created by
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
loaded from
.IR $HOME/.euclid/credentials .
Like
.BR eqs (1)
and
.BR esm (1)
requests, they are signed with SigV4 using the stored access key ID and
secret if present, falling back to the bearer token otherwise.
.PP
If the server rejects a request with
.IR "HTTP 401" ,
run
.B euclid-cli eam login
again.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The action completed successfully.
.TP
.B 1
Argument parsing failed, the request could not be sent, or the server
rejected it (missing/expired session, invalid input, etc.). Details are
printed to standard error.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $HOME/.euclid/credentials
JSON file holding the current session's bearer token and/or SigV4
access key, created by
.B euclid-cli eam login
and read by every
.B ekm
action.
.SH EXAMPLES
Create a key and list keys:
.PP
.RS
.nf
euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm create-key \e
    --algorithm aes-gcm --length 256

euclid-cli --endpoint http://localhost:5566 ekm list-keys
.fi
.RE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR euclid-cli (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam (1),
.BR euclid-cli-eam-login (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-create-key (1),
.BR euclid-cli-ekm-list-keys (1)
